+// Avnir guest-facing GPU identity (Apache-2.0). Install what the renderer tells the GUEST its GPU
+// is. See the doc comment on struct stream_renderer_gpu_identity for the sentinel convention and
+// the must-be-called-before-init rule.
+//
+// This is a pure transport: validate the ABI, copy the fields across, done. It makes no decision
+// about any value, which is the whole design — the policy lives in the VMM (AEmulator's
+// `aemulator-identity` crate) where it is testable Rust, and this side cannot silently disagree with
+// it. An init parameter was rejected because stream_renderer_param::value is a bare uint64_t (no
+// room for a 256-byte name or a 16-byte UUID, and no struct_size to version), and an environment
+// variable was rejected because this repo already carries driver_pin.rs in its entirety as the
